        "math_academy_id": "q-76202",
        "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i} & 4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $bc+eg?$",
        "worked_solution": "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i} & 4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8+0\\text{i} & 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i} & 4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $b=1,c=3,e=0$ and $g=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nbc+eg=1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 1=3.\n$$",
